{"kind":"request","text":"Security R6 and R7, and finding 3.4 (6dd06d03 sections 2.2, 3.2-3.4 and 5): versions and extents.\n\nWork:\n1. R6. Creation of a new scope accepts only the newest cohort, plus the versions that live scopes of the deployment already pin. Name how the deployment lists those versions. Raise the defaults to the newest versions (at review time: membership@8, rules@10, directory@16; check the numbers at the head). Live scopes keep their pinned versions (2.2).\n2. R7, in the next rules version. At activate: refuse `approvals` below 1 unless an explicit opt-in field says so; restrict `approver` to review actions; refuse an extent pattern that matches no path, unless an explicit field marks it for a future path; make `ownerMayReview` explicit, with no default (3.2, 3.3).\n3. Finding 3.4. When extents exist, a check marked `required` is enforced at the destination, or the lane refreshes its rules copy before each judgment that depends on it. State which (packages/scope/src/reservation.ts:267-286; apps/room/lanes/src/change.ts:1290-1328).\n\nWitnesses: an old version is refused for a new scope and accepted for a live scope that pins it; each extents refusal with its reason; a rules activation without `ownerMayReview` refused; a required check enforced with a stale lane copy of the rules.\n\nCloses 2.2, 3.2, 3.3 and 3.4. The rules version bump is the planner's to schedule with the grow demo's cohort; the head's report says which live scopes it affects.\n\nCommon conditions (6dd06d03, review of main 603220b9). Checker review of each exact head before it lands. A head can close part of this request; each head names the findings it closes. The hosted Workers (artroom-scope, dap-grow, dap-lending) stay deployable after each head: the head's report lists every new setting and redeploy step, and the planner deploys after review. No deployment by the builder. Place in the security order: 8 of 10 (6dd06d03 assert lists the order). The archive slices keep priority when one of them is ready to work: F1, 9a, slice 9, F2 (land by 4 November) and F3 (deploy by 6 November).","body":{"conditions":"Newest cohort only for creation, newer defaults, extents refusals in the next rules version, explicit ownerMayReview, required checks enforced with extents; closes 2.2, 3.2, 3.3, 3.4. Checker review on every head; hosted Workers stay deployable; no builder deployment.","target":"inherit","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}